HowToUse.MainPurpose=The main purpose of this application is to get a svg version of the glyph you select to any vector editing software.
HowToUse.GetSvg=In order to get a svg version of a glyph first select a font you like, select the character weight, style and stretch, set the desired character size in the 'Output' text box. You can choose if you want an outlined version of the character by clicking in the checkbox labeled 'Outlined'. Then drag a symbol from this application to the desired vector editing software. Every time you change the font the screen below will list every character that is available for the selected item.
HowToUse.GetSvgFile=You can also drag a glyph to a folder or the desktop to get a svg file of the character you started dragging.
HowToUse.ChangeTheme=You can change the theme of the application by selecting Theme > Dark.
HowToUse.ExportAll=By clicking on the 'Export All' button and then selecting a folder from the appeared window, you can export every character for the font, style, stretch, weight, characters size you specified, and if the checkbox with label 'Outlined' is checked then the characters will be outlined. If the button is green, that means there is an active export at the moment. 
Tooltip.OpenTypeInfo=OpenType font weights